MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_001: *yawn* So sleepy... No, Lulu! Resist it! Imagine if\nsomeone caught you yawning!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_002: Too late! I saw you. So what's the story? Late night?
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_003: E-Esmeralda?! It's true... I got so wrapped up in the\nbook I was reading, it was morning before I knew it!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_004: But that just tells you how good it is! It's about a boy\nfrom the slums who finds a talking stone one day...
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_005: And surprise! The stone says it's inhabited by the\nspirit of a princess! So the boy takes it on a journey...
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_006: Wait. Hold on. It's not like I'm going to say I'm sorry\nI asked, but... That's plenty, thanks.
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_007: What do you mean? You don't wish something\namazing and unbelievable like that happened to you?
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_008: So far, my life has been so full of unbelievable things\nI can barely keep up. I don't think I need books.
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_009: Back in my village, they called me a demon. They\ntried to sacrifice me—I nearly died!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_010: But then Sweetie saved me. Well, I guess it was\nFabio who saved me. Ludia? You OK?
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_011: Oh! It's like something out of a storybook! I was\njust swept away!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_012: With a life like that, I can see how you wouldn't\nwant for more...
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_013: But then what do you do during your down time\nto keep from getting bored?
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_014: Well, I carve dolls. Ever since I was young... On\nrainy days, when there's no work to do. 
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_015: Back then, I'd use cast-offs from the boatbuilders.\nNowadays, I grab things like broken spear shafts.
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_016: Huh! I didn't expect that. Would you be up for\nshowing me a few?
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_017: Sure, why not?
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_018: Whoa! Is this one Dietrich?! This one HAS to\nbe Fabio...
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_019: They're so lifelike! I bet you could make some\nmoney selling these... I could help, if you like!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_020: No, that's OK. I don't really want money. Anyway,\nit's just a hobby. Take whatever you want.
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_021: No, I couldn't! Though, they're so nice, it'd be\na shame for them to go to waste... Oh, I've got it!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_022: Esmeralda, do you know how to carve things that\naren't people? Like, say, skeletons?
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_023: I think so... Why do you ask? Do you...like skeletons?
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_C_024: Hehehe. Oh, you'll see! Just you wait. I'll get\nback to you!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_001: Esme, these are amazing! And you've even given\nthe skeletons their own personalities!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_002: Well, it'd be boring to just keep carving the same\nface over and over. 
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_003: With that, preparations are complete! We're ready\nfor a puppet show. The local kids came to watch too!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_004: Puppets? A play? I just make dolls! I don't know\nhow to put on a play!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_005: Don't worry! The dolls have plenty of personality on\ntheir own. We just need to attach some sticks!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_006: As for the acting, you'll be playing yourself. I wrote\nthe script based on your life! This is your story!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_007: Wait, wait, wait... My story? A script? But you don't\nknow my story! I just hinted at a couple of things...
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_008: I filled in the rest of the details with my imagination.\nA beautiful swordsman and a creepy missionary...
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_009: And a powerful female lead! Together, they solve\nmysteries plaguing a haunted village.
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_010: Villagers disappear, one after the other, but they all\nhave one thing in common...
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_011: Before disappearing, each of them said they'd seen\nsomeone who looked like they could be their twin!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_012: Ooh, creepy! The idea of meeting your double...\nI just know Sweetie would be interested!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_013: I bet you want to know who's behind it all, right?!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_014: You know what? I'll do it! If you'll have me, I'd love\nto take part in your play!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_015: I am beat! I thought I had stamina, but that was too\nstressful for words.
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_016: Haha! Same here... But it was a roaring success!\nEven the adults were enjoying it!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_017: Did you hear the crowd? When they figured out it\nwas the headman using Drake's treasures all along...
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_018: Well, he was the first to disappear, right? And he\nseemed so timid...until he was found out, that is!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_019: Turning into Fabio and trying to trick everybody!\nBut I sniffed him out!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_020: Then, when he tried to overrun the village with\nskeletons...Sweetie cut them down. Of course!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_021: Ehe. I'm glad you enjoyed it as much as I did.\nIt was fun, right?
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_022: It was! You're really something else, Ludia.\nWriting a play, putting it on with my dolls.
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_023: Well, after hearing your story and seeing your dolls,\nI just had to bring the idea to life!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_024: But I do appreciate the compliment. Thank you.
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_025: No thanks necessary. In fact, thanks to you, I learned\njust how much fun stories like this are!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_026: If you want to put on more plays, I can keep making\ndolls. I'd like to see what you come up with!
MID_SE_Esm_Lou_B_027: Really? Deal! And when I'm a famous puppet-show\nplaywright, you'll get the best seats in the house!